// The Album des Pavillons 2000's construction, as FOTW reports it: (9+2+2+2+9):(21+2+2+2+21),
// so 24 by 48. Its disc, as measured there, is 12 across.
// The stars are measured from the Commons drawing: on its 7200 hoist each has points at 1600.6
// and 1147.2 out from the center, so radius 453.4 / 1.809 = 250.6, centered 1350 out.
// Scaled by 24/7200: radius 0.835 on a ring of radius 4.5, each with a point outward.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Dominica"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "LicenseRef-Public-Domain"
  adapted-from "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Dominica.svg" {
    author "Wikimedia Commons contributors, listed in the file's history"
    license "LicenseRef-Public-Domain"
    part "the parrot and twig"
  }
  source "https://presidentoffice.gov.dm/images/symbols_of_nationhood.pdf"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20250124071355/https://presidentoffice.gov.dm/national-flag"
  source "https://www.crwflags.com/fotw/flags/dm.html"
  note "The Act's text wasn't read. Its number and dates, and the terms of its schedule, are from FOTW, and from the government's booklet The Symbols of Nationhood (1988), which gives the same blazon: green, with a cross of three conjoined stripes of gold, silver and black, and over all a red disc with a Sisserou parrot on a twig, in a ring of ten mullets, also green."
  note "The 2:1 proportion is the government's booklet, which isn't a law. The cross is the Album des Pavillons 2000's construction, as reported on FOTW, and the disc is a FOTW contributor's measurement of the Album's image. FOTW records other sizes, and flags disagree."
  note "The drawing of the parrot and twig is from the Commons file, not the law. The stars are drawn here as the blazon says, in the field's own color, with sizes measured from that drawing. The drawing's thin black outline on them isn't in the blazon and is left out. FOTW reports that a yellow edging on the stars was dropped."
  note "The hex, Pantone and CMYK values are the Album des Pavillons 2023's, as reported by FOTW."
  note "Commons' author field names Alwin Bully, which appears to be who made the design or passed the law rather than who drew this file."
  law "National Emblems of Dominica Act, Act No. 18 of 1978, Schedule, Part II"
}
palette {
  green "#169b62" {
    pantone "347 C"
    cmyk 81 12 76 1
  }
  yellow "#ffcc00" {
    pantone "116 C"
    cmyk 0 21 93 0
  }
  white "#ffffff"
  black "#000000"
  red "#c8102e" {
    pantone "186 C"
    cmyk 14 100 79 4
  }
}
proportion hoist=24 fly=48

field green
cross yellow {
  fly 21 2 25
  hoist 9 2 13
}
cross black {
  fly 23 2 23
  hoist 11 2 11
}
cross white {
  fly 25 2 21
  hoist 13 2 9
}
charge disc red {
  radius 6
}
charge star green {
  radius 0.835
  repeat ring count=10 radius=4.5 turn=#true
}

charge svg {
  at center
  fly 48
  hoist 24
  markup #"""
